    <item>
      <title>The Envy of Ahalya, the Unyielding</title>
      <description>Today&apos;s story will change how you see everything... In the forest of Naimisha, a great sage named Rishyasringa was born with supernatural powers. His mother, a beautiful apsara named Vrisha, had been cursed by the gods to be born as a monkey. Rishyasringa&apos;s father, a sage named Vibhandaka, raised him in isolation. But when the king of Anga, Dasaratha, heard of the boy&apos;s powers, he sought to marry Rishyasringa&apos;s sister, Shanta. Ahalya, the king&apos;s beautiful wife, grew envious of Shanta&apos;s beauty and the king&apos;s attention towards the sage&apos;s sister. She began to plot against Shanta, sending her away from the kingdom. But the gods, in their infinite wisdom, had other plans. They sent a great sage, Agastya, to marry Ahalya, hoping to bring peace to the kingdom. But Ahalya&apos;s envy only grew stronger. She began to plot against Agastya, trying to destroy his reputation. But the sage&apos;s wisdom and the gods&apos; protection saved him. Ahalya&apos;s envy destroyed her, and she was cursed by the gods to be a ghost, invisible to all but the wise sage who would eventually redeem her. This is Envy — the poison that consumes your soul. Ask yourself, what&apos;s the price of your own shadow?</description>
      <pubDate>Sat, 11 Apr 2026 13:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
